The purpose of the app is to help set up program rules that validat dates in DHIS2 tracker programmes.

**Key components:**
* Selector where the tracker programme can be selected
* Overview page listing all date variables for the programme:
  * Render enrollment (date teas), program stages, sections and **date** data elements in some structure way. For example collapsible sections per program stage. Also including the enrollment, due (if applicable), incidence (if applicable) and program stage event dates - using any custom labels configured for the programme.
  * For each date, some indication of whether validations already exists for each variable.
* Details page for a particular date variables/attribute/dataElement
  * show current validations for that data element, meaning rules with “show warning” or “show error” actions
  * list separately any program rules that the variable is used in (for reference)
  * an interface to add new date validation program rules, or editing existing ones (when possible), which lets the user set up validation from a predifined list of options (see types of validation below)

**Types of validation for dates:**
* Date A should be on or before date B
* Date A should be before date B
* Date A should be on or after date B
* Date A should be after date B
* Difference between Date A and Date B should be less than (or equal to) X days/months/years (use d2:daysBetween, d2:monthsBetween etc program rule expression functions)
* Difference between Date A and Date B should be more than (or equal to) X days/months/years (use d2:daysBetween, d2:monthsBetween etc program rule expression functions)
For before/on/after validation, the expression can be configured as `d2:daysBetween(date a, date b) </<=/>/=> 0`
For “difference” validation, the expression can be `d2:days/months/yearsBetween(date a, date b) </<=/>/=> X`
Dates here can be data elements, tracked entity attributes, or built in variables (event data, enrollment date etc)

**Types of warning:**
* Show warning
* Show error
* Show warning on complete
* Show errorn on complete

The name and description of the program rule should have a default value populated, based on the specific dates in question, e.g.
“Date validation: Vaccination date should be on or after Date of birth”, if the two variables checkes are “Vaccination date” and “Date of birth”.

The app should have a “settings” modal where standard prefixes can be set per programme, stored in the DHIS2 dataStore, and used on subsequent loading of the app. E.g. the user might specify that the immunisation registry should have a standard “EIR - “ prefix to the name, and that program rule variables should have EIR_ prefix” etc.

Important notes:
* In the program rule expressions, we should always add check to ensure any dates being compared have values (at least the one being validated).
* Note that in program rule expressions, data elements and tracked entity attributes cannot be used directly, but must be added as programRuleVariables first, if they don’t already exists. In this app, only “Data element in current event” and “Tracked entity attribute” sources are relevant for programRuleVariables. Only add new PRVs when they are needed for a program rules being created.

**Example flow**
* App opens, with drop down of programs loaded
* Users selects a program
  * Config for that program is shown, e.g. standard prefix - or an empty one if this is the first time the program is loaded
    * User saves these settings to datastore
  * all relevant metadata for that program is fetched from the DHIS2 api
* A list of date variables for the selcted programme is shown in a user friendly and structured way, including an indication of whether there is already validation configured for that variable
* Users chooses one of the date variables for which validation should be configured
* A page is loaded for that particular variable where validations can be set up
* In the details page the users sees any validations configured currently, and can add/edit/remove validations
* When saving, the updates are first validated and if successfull submitted to the server
* The user is back at the overview page and can set up validation for the next date
